content.summary_of_the_paper:
This paper starts with investigating the decoding speed and Mask strategies on both AT and NAT models. According to their findings, they propose a hybrid-regressive method to take advantages of AT and NAT models into account for keeping the decoding quality and efficiency at once.  This model is trained on the multi-task framework with curriculum learning and mixed distillation technical. In the inference process, this model adopts a two-stage generation strategy. They first autoregressively generate the start words of each chunk, then use a NAT decoder to recover all the masks in each chunk. 

The contributions of this work:
1. Learning the acceleration robustness problem in IR-NAT;
2. Investigating the effectiveness of masking ratio on the inference process;
3. They proposed a hybrid-regressive method to balance the advantages of AT and NAT;
4. The proposed method outperforms the baseline on three language pairs in both speed and quality of generation.
